# Cloudflare Pages redirect rules
#
# Goal: collapse every non-canonical URL variant into a SINGLE 301 hop
# to https://flotionrecords.com/<path>. Without these rules, a request
# like http://www.flotionrecords.com/services.html would chain through
# http→https, www→apex, and .html→extensionless — three hops, which
# Google Search Console flags as "Fout met omleiding".
#
# The trailing ! forces these rewrites over the default 200 that Pages
# would otherwise serve for the same path.

# 1. http + www  → https + apex (single hop, prevents 2-hop chain)
http://www.flotionrecords.com/* https://flotionrecords.com/:splat 301!

# 2. https + www → https + apex
https://www.flotionrecords.com/* https://flotionrecords.com/:splat 301!

# 3. Strip .html extension at the source (one hop instead of Cloudflare's
#    follow-up 308). Only fires when the request lands on the apex.
/*.html /:splat 301!
